      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression of the HA-tagged construct was confirmed by anti-HA staining in surface-expression and trafficking assays; electrophysiological function of the tagged channel is not explicitly reported for the tag-bearing construct itself.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 directly reports a full-length, membrane-anchored human KCNA2 construct with an HA epitope inserted in the extracellular loop between S1 (TM1, 164-182) and S2 (TM2, 222-242), which by the authoritative topology landmarks corresponds to residues 183-221. No specific junction residue is named in either L1 or L2, so insert_after_residue is left null and the site is classified as region-level. The loop is 39 residues long and fully extracellular, providing ample space for a short epitope tag. The N-terminal EGFP/mRFP1 fusions in the same constructs are intracellular and are recorded separately in other_positions. Full-length human KV1.2 (KCNA2) constructs bearing an N-terminal EGFP or mRFP1 fusion and an extracellular HA tag inserted 'between transmembrane helices S1 and S2' were used for surface-expression studies in transfected cells (L1). A parallel rat Kv1.2 construct with the same S1-S2 HA insertion was used for surface trafficking studies (L2, indirect). Neither paper names a specific residue junction within the loop.",
      "sources": [
